      "id": "53c27649-c920-549e-8926-19d886c07ba9",
      "name": "Run Target per Email",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "alwaysOutputData": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One result per run, shown here and returned to a caller.\n// A failed email does not stop the run: the target's error arrives here as an item.\n// The loop runs the target once per email, so run r of the target belongs to email r.\nconst sent = $('Stop If Dry Run').all();\nconst errors = [];\nfor (let r = 0; r < sent.length; r++) {\n  let out = [];\n  try { out = $('Run Target per Email').all(0, r); } catch (e) { break; }\n  const bad = out.find(i => i.json.error);\n  if (bad) errors.push({ id: sent[r].json.id ?? 'unknown', error: bad.json.error });\n}\nconst found = $('Search Gmail Messages').all().length;\nreturn [{ json: {\n  query: $('Config').first().json.query,\n  found,\n  processed: sent.length - errors.length,\n  failed: errors.length,\n  // found but not sent this run, because of max_emails. Run again to continue.\n  left_for_next_run: found - sent.length,\n  errors: errors.slice(0, 20),\n} }];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        1680,
        288
      ],
      "id": "0ac569dd-ea5a-59aa-b783-96337dfa85b5",
      "name": "Summarize Run",
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Gmail batch processor\n\n### How it works\n1. Takes a Gmail search, a time range and a target workflow from **Config**. A calling workflow can override any of them.\n2. Splits the time range into date windows, so a large mailbox is fetched in small pieces.\n3. Searches Gmail in each window.\n4. Runs the target workflow once per email, one after another. A failing email is counted, not fatal.\n5. Returns a summary: found, processed, failed, left for the next run.\n\nIt holds no rules of its own: no whitelist, no labels. Every decision stays in the target.\n\n### Setup\n- [ ] Connect your Gmail credential to **Search Gmail Messages**\n- [ ] Set `target_workflow_id` in **Config** to the ID of your inbox attachment organizer (the default is the author's)\n- [ ] Click **Execute workflow**. The output of **Summarize Run** shows `left_for_next_run`: click again until it is `0`\n- [ ] More than about 40 emails: use a paid LLM tier in the target. On a free tier set `max_emails: 25` and `rate_limit_wait_seconds: 45`\n\n### Customization\nThe default `query` finds the emails the organizer missed: never processed, or stuck on `inProgress`. Change `query` and `target_workflow_id` to run any workflow over any set of emails. Want a way back first? Run `gmail-backup`.\n",
        "height": 800,
        "width": 480
      },
